2. Running Compose from wrong directory
Your input:
docker compose up -d --build

Output:
no configuration file provided: not found

What this means
Docker Compose looks for:
docker-compose.yml

in the current directory.
You were in:

/home/ec2-user

but your project was:
/home/ec2-user/devops-exam-portal

Fix:
Navigate into the project:
cd devops-exam-portal

Then:
docker compose up -d --build

3. Missing environment variables
Your input:
MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD variable is not set
DB_NAME variable is not set
.env not found

What I checked
Docker Compose was expecting:
.env

because your compose file referenced variables.
Example:

environment:
  MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: ${MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD}

Docker replaces:
${MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD}

from:
.env

Debug commands:
Check files:
ls -la

Look for:
.env
.env.example
.env.sample

If missing:
cp .env.example .env

4. Buildx error during image build
Your input:
compose build requires buildx 0.17.0 or later

What I identified
Docker Compose v2 uses BuildKit/Buildx to build images.
The issue was:

Docker Buildx plugin missing or outdated

Debug commands:
docker buildx version
docker version

Possible fix:
Install/update Buildx.

