8. Login failed debugging
You reported:
login failed

First question:
"Is backend receiving the request?"

Checked:

docker compose logs -f backend

Output:
Database connected.
Server running on port 5001

No login request appeared.
Reasoning:
If backend does not show login request:
Possible causes:

Frontend not calling backend
Wrong API URL
Proxy problem
9. Checking frontend API configuration
Command:
grep -R "localhost\|5001\|api" frontend/

Found:
frontend/nginx.conf:

proxy_pass http://backend:5000/api/

Important discovery.
Frontend was sending:

Frontend nginx
       |
       |
       backend:5000

But backend actually runs:
backend:5001

From:
docker compose ps

we saw:
5001->5001

and from:
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 5001;

Therefore:
Wrong:

backend:5000 ❌

Correct:
backend:5001 ✅

10. Confirming the problem from frontend logs
Command:
docker compose logs frontend --tail=100

Found:
POST /api/auth/login

upstream:
http://172.22.0.3:5000/api/auth/login

connect() failed (111: Connection refused)

This confirmed:
Frontend proxy was wrong.

11. Fix
Changed:
proxy_pass http://backend:5000/api/;

to:
proxy_pass http://backend:5001/api/;

Then rebuilt:
docker compose up -d --build frontend

